# Copy to .env and fill in whichever you have. The system runs with any subset;
# keys can also be entered on the Settings screen in the UI.
#
# Provider ids match server/agentzero/agent/providers.py
#
# A provider can hold more than one key -- useful when its rate limits are
# per-key rather than per-account (NVIDIA, Mistral, Google AI Studio and
# OpenRouter are; Groq's are per-organisation, so a second Groq key won't
# raise its real ceiling even though it's still picked up). Add more with a
# numbered suffix, in order, with no gaps:
#   GROQ_API_KEY=
#   GROQ_API_KEY_2=
#   GROQ_API_KEY_3=
# Keys entered here and keys typed into the Settings screen are merged, not
# one overriding the other -- both count toward the same provider's rotation.
NVIDIA_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
MISTRAL_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
COHERE_API_KEY=
# Local Ollama needs no key; set the base url only if it is not the default.
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# Optional: powers the web_search tool (https://exa.ai). Without it, the
# executor is told web search isn't configured and continues without it --
# nothing else in the system requires this key.
EXA_API_KEY=
